  5. Switch Clerk to Production Instance                                                                                                                                                                  
                                                            
  Clerk has separate dev and production instances. The dev instance has a localhost-only JWT issuer. You must create a Clerk production app and get new keys for NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY,
  CLERK_SECRET_KEY, and CLERK_JWT_ISSUER.    

  Clerk Production Instance                                                                                                                                                                      
                                                                                                                                                                                                          
  In the Clerk Dashboard                                                                                                                                                                                  
                                                                                                                                                                                                          
  1. Create a production application
  - Go to https://clerk.com → your app → top-left dropdown → "Create application" (or switch the existing one from Development to Production)                                                             
  - Clerk keeps dev and prod completely separate — different keys, different user databases                                                                                                               
                                                                                           
  2. Set your production domain                                                                                                                                                                           
  - In the production app: Domains → add contiq.app (your frontend domain)                                                                                                                                
  - Clerk will give you a DNS record to add — a CNAME at something like clerk.contiq.app                                                                                                                  
  - Add that record in your domain registrar (Cloudflare/Namecheap)                                                                                                                                       
                                                                                                                                                                                                          
  3. Get the production keys                                                                                                                                                                              
  - API Keys section gives you:                                                                                                                                                                           
    - NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY — starts with pk_live_... (dev is pk_test_...)                                                                                                                    
    - CLERK_SECRET_KEY — starts with sk_live_...                                                                                                                                                          
  - JWT Templates → note the issuer URL (looks like https://clerk.contiq.app or https://your-instance.clerk.accounts.dev for prod)                                                                        
   
  ---                                                                                                                                                                                                     
  Environment Variables to Set                              
                                                                                                                                                                                                          
  Frontend (Vercel env vars):                               
  NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_live_...                                                                                                                                                           
  CLERK_SECRET_KEY=sk_live_...                              
  NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_SIGN_IN_URL=/auth/sign-in                                                                                                                                                             
  NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_SIGN_UP_URL=/auth/sign-up               
  NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_AFTER_SIGN_IN_URL=/dashboard                                                                                                                                                          
  NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_AFTER_SIGN_UP_URL=/dashboard
  NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://api.contiq.app                                                                                                                                                              
                                                                                                                                                                                                          
  Backend (Railway env vars):
  CLERK_SECRET_KEY=sk_live_...                                                                                                                                                                            
  CLERK_JWT_ISSUER=https://clerk.contiq.app                                                                                                                                                               
                                           
  The CLERK_JWT_ISSUER is what auth.py uses to fetch JWKS keys for verifying tokens:                                                                                                                      
  jwks_url = f"{settings.CLERK_JWT_ISSUER}/.well-known/jwks.json"                                                                                                                                         
  So it must exactly match the issuer in your Clerk production JWT — you can verify it by decoding a token at https://jwt.io and checking the iss claim.
                                                                                                                                                                                                          
  ---                                                                                                                                                                                                     
  One Thing to Watch                                                                                                                                                                                      
                                                                                                                                                                                                          
  Your dev users won't carry over to production — Clerk's prod instance starts with an empty user database. That's expected and correct. Anyone who signed up during dev testing will need to sign up
  again on the production domain.                                                                                                                                                                         
   
                                                                                                                                                             
   
