  ---
  14. Error Tracking — Sentry                                                                                                                                                                             
                                                            
  Currently errors just print() to console. In production you need alerts. Sentry has a generous free tier:
  - Frontend: @sentry/nextjs                                                                                                                                                                              
  - Backend: sentry-sdk[fastapi]
  - ~2 hours to integrate                                                                                                                                                                                 

   To activate in production

  1. Create a free Sentry account at https://sentry.io → New Project → Next.js (frontend) + Python/FastAPI (backend — create as a separate project)

  2. Add to production env vars:

  Backend (Railway):
  SENTRY_DSN=https://xxx@oyyy.ingest.sentry.io/zzz
  ENVIRONMENT=production

  Frontend (Vercel):
  NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=https://xxx@oyyy.ingest.sentry.io/zzz
  SENTRY_ORG=your-org-slug
  SENTRY_PROJECT=contiq-frontend
  SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN=your-auth-token   # from Sentry → Settings → Auth Tokens

  What you get:
  - Every unhandled exception in FastAPI automatically sent to Sentry with full stack trace
  - Frontend JS errors captured with the component stack
  - SENTRY_DSN empty in dev → Sentry completely off, zero overhead locally
  - Source maps uploaded on production builds so Sentry shows your actual TypeScript code, not minified output

